SUMMARY:Beyond the Basics: Deer Hunting Land & Sign: How to Choose Where—and How—to Hunt (Online)
DESCRIPTION:Join NCWF Fall Line Outdoors Chapter and find your place in the woods. Learn how to locate public and private hunting opportunities\, use digital maps with confidence\, and obtain landowner permission. Build scouting skills by understanding habitat\, food sources\, deer behavior\, topography\, wind and thermals\, and travel corridors. Compare stand types\, weigh pros and cons\, and reinforce safe elevated‑stand practices. You’ll leave ready to identify good deer habitat\, choose effective stand sites\, and hunt safely. \nREGISTER HERE
URL:https://ncwf.org/event/deer-hunting-how-to/
CATEGORIES:Featured
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://ncwf.org/wp-content/uploads/land.jpg
END:VEVENT
